<article class="env-remark" id="790310">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/790310">Remark <span data-tag="790310">8.3.2.6</span>.</a> The model structure of Proposition <a href="/tag/5606B3" data-tag="5606B3">8.3.2.4</a> enjoys the following functoriality: suppose that $f: \mathbf{S}\rightarrow \mathbf{S}'$ is a monoidal left Quillen functor between model categories satisfying the hypotheses of Proposition <a href="/tag/5606B3" data-tag="5606B3">8.3.2.4</a>, with right adjoint $g: \mathbf{S}' \rightarrow \mathbf{S}$. Then $f$ and $g$ induce a Quillen adjunction </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix {\SCat  \ar @< .4ex>[r]^{ F} &amp;  \Cat _{\mathbf{S}'}, \ar @< .4ex>[l]^{G}} \]
</div>
  <p> where $F$ and $G$ are as in Remark <a href="/tag/294A7A" data-tag="294A7A">8.1.4.3</a>. Moreover, if $(f,g)$ is a Quillen equivalence, then $(F,G)$ is likewise a Quillen equivalence. </p>
</article>